\section{End-to-End Integration Testing}

To validate that the individual components operate correctly as a unified system, a thirteen-case end-to-end integration test suite (\texttt{tests/test\_e2e.py}) was developed. The suite starts against a running orchestrator instance and exercises four layers: the data layer (presence and quality of training data), the model layer (presence of all six serialized artifacts and evaluation outputs), the API layer (every REST endpoint with representative inputs), and a full cross-model pipeline that drives a single failure build through prediction, anomaly detection, and CPU forecasting in sequence. All thirteen tests pass. Table~\ref{table:e2e} summarizes the suite and representative observed outputs.

